# Kids Portal constraints

- Before any implementation, read `PROGRESS.md` and claim one task id. Do not start work that is not on the board.
- After any implementation, update that task’s checkbox, `Active`, `Updated`, and Log in `PROGRESS.md`.
- Stack is Vite + React + TypeScript + Tailwind + Firebase (Auth, Firestore, Storage, Functions, Hosting) + PWA.
- Build only the current phase in `PROGRESS.md`. Do not implement later modules “while you are here.”
- Never write `members.balance` or `ledgerTransactions` from client code. Use callable Cloud Functions and Firestore transactions.
- One parent Firebase Auth session per device. Children are `members` documents, switched locally, with an optional 4-digit PIN for senior/parent.
- Junior and senior share the same schema. `members.tier` changes UI only.
- Work-order chat is nested under the work order. No global kid messenger.
- UI copy: Missions (junior), Work Orders (senior/parent), Stars, Spend/Save/Give, Parent Console, Family Marketplace.
- After UI or flow changes, verify in the browser. Do not stop at a screenshot.

Load `kids-portal-progress` first, then `kids-portal-product`, `kids-portal-firebase`, `kids-portal-ui`, `kids-portal-milestones` as needed.
